            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I do not like this at all. too magical. We are not trying to reinvent javascript or a 90:s database (still in use in 2026) where a person named \"John Null\" is cancelled from official existence.\r\n\r\nThe OBJECT typesystem is a typesystem that we own and define by ourselves. it is not a yak stack of hackarounds around previous ossified typesystems.\r\n\r\n**If** this is ever is supported, this must be supported natively in the core data structure so that number keys are **structurally** distinct from string keys in a `Dictionary`. and that is still an \"if\" to resolve before spending more effort into this (and the extra maintenance cost). ",
            "commit_id": "d4cedeb479331d8bc6cb5e703426348793ca62ee",
            "created_at": "2026-10-01T12:06:23Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -637,6 +640,48 @@ String copy_string(String str, Arena *arena)\n   }\n }\n \n+/// Try to parse a synthetic `__unkeyed-<n>` key.\n+/// Returns `true` on success, if `key` is a synthetic `__unkeyed-<n>` key.\n+///\n+/// @see UNKEYED_KEY_PREFIX\n+bool unkeyed_key_parse(String key, int64_t *out)",
