        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Looks like more trouble than it's worth. Is it blocking something, i.e. is it motivated by a use-case that really needs it? The example in https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/35550 can be \"fixed\" simply by putting the list data in a key:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_exec_autocmds(\"User\", { pattern = \"TestEvent\",\r\n  data = {\r\n    values = { a = { \"a\", \"b\" }, c = \"d\", },\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor passing custom event data around, plugins should easily be able to control that.\r\n\r\nThere might be an RPC use-case where the data source is not so easily controlled, though.",
            "created_at": "2026-09-30T22:27:50Z",
