            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Is it blocking something, i.e. is it motivated by a use-case that really needs it?\r\n\r\ntbh, I don't think so.\r\nThis came from Lua plugins leaning on Lua's table/list duality (e.g. lazy.nvim's `keys` spec, which I carried over into lz.n, a lazy-loading library that's plugin-manager-agnostic).\r\nThe only real argument is surprise: a Lua table passed to a Lua consumer through a Lua API fails with a confusing msgpack-conversion error.\r\n\r\nThis hack treats the symptom but adds complexity.\r\nIf we don't go with it, we should at least improve the error (e.g. along the lines of: `Invalid 'data': Cannot convert given Lua table: Integer keys in a mixed table aren't supported, see :help lua-table-ambiguous.`).\r\nAnd we'd probably want to warn plugin authors in `:h lua-plugin` not to build APIs around mixed list/tables if we can't support it properly.",
            "created_at": "2026-09-30T23:21:46Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42185#issuecomment-5921454274",
